{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pkgen2HKc8t57xJc1Z4TpA","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though specific dedicated reviewer guidelines and review form documentation for 2026 don't appear to be fully published yet. Here's what I found:\n\n## Current CoRL 2026 Information\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer. They are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ ICRA/ IROS/ RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/ NeurIPS/ ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\nAdditionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n## Review Process Guidelines\n\nWhile full 2026 guidelines may not yet be finalized, past CoRL conferences have provided detailed reviewer guidance. Based on CoRL 2024, submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nFor submissions, reviewers assess factors including:\n- Relevance: Does the paper address a problem in robot learning? Does it apply or improve a learning-based method, or a learned model? Is the method evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both? Will the CoRL audience be interested in reading this paper?\n\n## Where to Find Detailed Information\n\nFor the most current and complete CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking:\n- The official CoRL 2026 website (corl.org)\n- The OpenReview submission portal for CoRL 2026\n- Contact the conference organizers directly\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2be1a920-1f7c-4c94-bc45-d01d7138d885","uuid":"7305dab5-cfed-4117-ac76-d03cb92bbb31","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:43:28.487Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01NuYJsSvzNMSEdq1r5ryRDr","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though specific dedicated reviewer guidelines and review form documentation for 2026 don't appear to be fully published yet. Here's what I found:\n\n## Current CoRL 2026 Information\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer. They are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ ICRA/ IROS/ RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/ NeurIPS/ ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\nAdditionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n## Review Process Guidelines\n\nWhile full 2026 guidelines may not yet be finalized, past CoRL conferences have provided detailed reviewer guidance. Based on CoRL 2024, submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nFor submissions, reviewers assess factors including:\n- Relevance: Does the paper address a problem in robot learning? Does it apply or improve a learning-based method, or a learned model? Is the method evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both? Will the CoRL audience be interested in reading this paper?\n\n## Where to Find Detailed Information\n\nFor the most current and complete CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking:\n- The official CoRL 2026 website (corl.org)\n- The OpenReview submission portal for CoRL 2026\n- Contact the conference organizers directly"],"durationSeconds":5.954094161000001}}
