{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016CWkKBC1fY8aYVQHBT4oHs","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews reviewer guidelines rating scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerInstructions\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page. Here's what I found regarding reviewer guidelines:\n\n## Reviewer Qualifications\n\nReviewers ideally have a minimum of 3 first author publications in major robotics conferences and journals (e.g. CoRL, RSS, ICRA, IROS, IJRR, TRO, RAL) and core machine learning venues (e.g. NeurIPS, ICML, AIStats, JMLR, PAMI).\n\n## Evaluation Criteria\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical. Results will be judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\n## Review Process\n\nAuthors of regular paper submissions will have an opportunity to submit a response to reviewers and update the papers during the rebuttal period.\n\nHowever, the search results I retrieved do not contain specific details about the numerical rating scale used for CoRL 2024 reviews. If you need more detailed information about the specific rating scale, I may need to search more specifically for that information.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2be1a920-1f7c-4c94-bc45-d01d7138d885","uuid":"52bcfa88-7a66-445d-a18f-e8c0c64a19c7","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:43:39.883Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews reviewer guidelines rating scale","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01NRt61r6gHuJDw5ojG7Lo4k","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions","url":"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerInstructions"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"}]},"Based on the search results, I found the CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page. Here's what I found regarding reviewer guidelines:\n\n## Reviewer Qualifications\n\nReviewers ideally have a minimum of 3 first author publications in major robotics conferences and journals (e.g. CoRL, RSS, ICRA, IROS, IJRR, TRO, RAL) and core machine learning venues (e.g. NeurIPS, ICML, AIStats, JMLR, PAMI).\n\n## Evaluation Criteria\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical. Results will be judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\n## Review Process\n\nAuthors of regular paper submissions will have an opportunity to submit a response to reviewers and update the papers during the rebuttal period.\n\nHowever, the search results I retrieved do not contain specific details about the numerical rating scale used for CoRL 2024 reviews. If you need more detailed information about the specific rating scale, I may need to search more specifically for that information."],"durationSeconds":8.341735448}}
